@page "/capabilities"

<PageTitle>What TokenSaver can do</PageTitle>

<section class="hero-small">
    <div class="hero-inner">
        <h1>What TokenSaver can do</h1>
        <p class="lead">
            A <strong>structural warm start</strong> for AI coding agents in
            <strong>.NET</strong>. Hand the model a cheap signature map of your
            code instead of whole files, so it reads only what it needs.
            Outlining a file saves <strong>70&nbsp;–&nbsp;95&nbsp;%</strong> of
            tokens versus reading it — the end-to-end win is biggest on smaller,
            cheaper models and large codebases.
        </p>
        <p class="how">
            Just talk to your AI in plain text — reference a file by path or
            ask about a method by name. TokenSaver picks the right tool
            behind the scenes.
        </p>
        <p class="how how-secondary">
            Some non-.NET file types (JS, TS, Python, HTML, CSS, JSON, YAML, XML, C++, X++)
            also have basic minification support, but those paths are not actively
            tested and results may vary.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="caveat">
    <div class="caveat-title">Read operations only</div>
    <p>
        TokenSaver shortens what the AI <em>reads</em>. It doesn't change how
        code is <em>written</em>. The tool output is a stripped-down view —
        comments and formatting are gone — so when the AI is about to edit
        your file, it usually has to re-read the original raw file to match
        the exact text on disk.
    </p>
    <p class="caveat-takeaway">
        Translation: big savings on understanding and discovery, smaller
        savings on edit-heavy tasks. That's intentional — accuracy matters
        more than tokens when code is changing.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="caveat caveat-info">
    <div class="caveat-title">First call in a session</div>
    <p>
        When an AI session starts, the model loads the server instructions and all tool
        descriptions before any tool is invoked — roughly <strong>4,200 tokens</strong> of fixed
        overhead. TokenSaver deducts this cost from the savings reported on the first tool call
        of each session, so the number you see is always the <em>net</em> saving, not a gross figure
        that ignores startup cost. Subsequent calls in the same session show full savings with no
        deduction.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="tools">
    <h2>The tools</h2>
    <p style="opacity:.75;font-size:.9rem;margin:.25rem 0 1.25rem;">
        Percentages are conservative: the focus tools are measured against reading just
        the relevant code (the method plus its helpers), while whole-file tools like
        outline and minify compare against the whole file. Measured against reading the
        entire file the focus figures are far higher — but a careful reader wouldn't load
        the whole file to answer a single-method question.
    </p>
<!-- BEGIN:generated:tools -->
<div class="tool-grid">
        <div class="tool-card">
            <div class="tool-name">Outline</div>
            <div class="tool-desc">Skeleton of a C# file — every type and member as a signature, no bodies. Best for navigation and discovery.</div>
            <div class="tool-example">&ldquo;What methods are on OrderService?&rdquo;</div>
            <div class="tool-savings">70 – 95 %</div>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-card">
            <div class="tool-name">Minify file</div>
            <div class="tool-desc">Auto-dispatches by extension. Covers every supported language — JS/TS, Python, HTML, CSS, JSON, YAML, XML, C, C++, and more. Falls back to lexical stripping for non-C# types.</div>
            <div class="tool-example">&ldquo;Read App.csproj — why is this package reference here?&rdquo;</div>
            <div class="tool-savings">20 – 50 %</div>
        </div>
        <div class="tool-card">
            <div class="tool-name">Trace DI registrations</div>
            <div class="tool-desc">Finds every Dependency-Injection registration for a type and returns a compact table — file:line, lifetime, and service → implementation. Answers "where is this wired, and to what?", which a constructor search can't, since DI types are never newed.</div>
            <div class="tool-example">&ldquo;Where is IOrderRepository registered, and what's it wired to?&rdquo;</div>
            <div class="tool-savings">50 – 80 %</div>
        </div>
    </div>
<!-- END:generated:tools -->
</section>

<section class="examples">
    <h2>Try saying things like…</h2>
    <p style="opacity:.75;font-size:.9rem;margin:.25rem 0 1.25rem;">
        Focus-tool percentages are conservative — measured against reading just the
        relevant code (the method plus the helpers it needs), not the whole file.
        Outline and minify compare against the whole file, since that is the real alternative.
    </p>

    @{bool shownAdditionalHeader = false;}
    @foreach (var ex in Examples)
    {
        @if (!ex.Primary && !shownAdditionalHeader)
        {
            shownAdditionalHeader = true;
            <div class="section-divider">
                <span>Additional support — basic minification, not actively tested</span>
            </div>
        }
        <div class="example-card @(ex.Primary ? "" : "example-card-secondary")">
            <div class="example-head">
                <span class="badge-lang">@ex.Language</span>
                <span class="badge-ext">@ex.Extensions</span>
                <span class="badge-savings @SavingsTier(ex.SavingsHigh)">@ex.SavingsLow – @ex.SavingsHigh % saved</span>
            </div>
            <div class="example-prompt">&ldquo;@ex.Prompt&rdquo;</div>
            <div class="example-explain">@ex.Explain</div>
        </div>
    }
</section>

<style>
    .hero-small {
        background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0d2b4e 0%, #1a4a7a 60%, #2d7dd2 100%);
        color: #fff;
        padding: 2.5rem 2rem;
        border-radius: 12px;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
        box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(13, 43, 78, 0.25);
    }

    .hero-small .hero-inner {
        max-width: 800px;
        margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .hero-small h1 {
        font-size: 2.25rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }

    .hero-small .lead {
        font-size: 1.15rem;
        margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
        opacity: 0.95;
    }

    .hero-small .lead strong {
        color: #b5f0c4;
    }

    .hero-small .how {
        margin: 0;
        opacity: 0.75;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    .caveat {
        border-left: 4px solid #d9a93c;
        background: #fff8e7;
        border-radius: 6px;
        padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .caveat.caveat-info {
        border-left-color: #2d7dd2;
        background: #f0f6ff;
    }

    .caveat.caveat-info .caveat-title {
        color: #1a4a7a;
    }

    .caveat-title {
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #8a6d1c;
        margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
        font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .caveat p {
        margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        color: #4a4a4a;
        line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .caveat p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

    .caveat-takeaway {
        font-style: italic;
        color: #5a5a5a;
    }

    .tools, .examples {
        margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }

    h2 {
        font-size: 1.3rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }

    .tool-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
        gap: 1rem;
    }

    .tool-card {
        border: 1px solid #e3e5e8;
        border-radius: 10px;
        padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
        background: #fff;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 0.5rem;
        transition: transform 0.12s ease, box-shadow 0.12s ease;
    }

    .tool-card:hover {
        transform: translateY(-2px);
        box-shadow: 0 6px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
    }

    .tool-name {
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        color: #1a4a7a;
    }

    .tool-desc {
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        color: #555;
        line-height: 1.4;
    }

    .tool-example {
        font-size: 0.82rem;
        font-style: italic;
        color: #888;
        border-top: 1px solid #eef0f3;
        padding-top: 0.4rem;
        margin-top: 0.1rem;
    }

    .tool-savings {
        margin-top: auto;
        font-weight: 700;
        font-size: 1.1rem;
        color: #2a9d4a;
        font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    }

    .example-card {
        border-left: 4px solid #2d7dd2;
        background: #f9fafc;
        border-radius: 6px;
        padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }

    .example-head {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 0.5rem;
        align-items: center;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .badge-lang {
        background: #1a4a7a;
        color: #fff;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        padding: 0.15rem 0.6rem;
        border-radius: 4px;
    }

    .badge-ext {
        font-family: ui-monospace, "Cascadia Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
        font-size: 0.78rem;
        color: #555;
        background: #eef0f3;
        padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
        border-radius: 4px;
    }

    .badge-savings {
        margin-left: auto;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        padding: 0.15rem 0.6rem;
        border-radius: 4px;
        font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    }

    .badge-savings.tier-high   { background: #d4f4dc; color: #1f7a37; }
    .badge-savings.tier-mid    { background: #fff2cc; color: #8a6d1c; }
    .badge-savings.tier-low    { background: #e7f1fd; color: #1a4a7a; }

    .example-prompt {
        font-style: italic;
        font-size: 1.02rem;
        color: #222;
        margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    }

    .example-explain {
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        color: #666;
    }

    .hero-small .how-secondary {
        margin-top: 0.6rem;
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        opacity: 0.65;
        font-style: italic;
    }

    .section-divider {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        margin: 1.5rem 0 0.75rem;
        color: #888;
        font-size: 0.82rem;
        font-style: italic;
    }

    .section-divider::before,
    .section-divider::after {
        content: "";
        flex: 1;
        border-top: 1px solid #dde1e7;
    }

    .example-card-secondary {
        border-left-color: #b0bec5;
        background: #f4f5f7;
        opacity: 0.85;
    }
</style>

@code {
    private record Example(
        string Language,
        string Extensions,
        string Prompt,
        string Explain,
        int SavingsLow,
        int SavingsHigh,
        bool Primary = true);

    private static readonly List<Example> Examples = new()
    {
        // ----- Primary: .NET / C# / Razor — fully supported and tested -----
        new("C# outline",
            ".cs",
            "What's in FocusedEmitter.cs?",
            "Outline tool returns just the type and method signatures — no bodies.",
            70, 95),

        new("C# trace DI registrations",
            ".cs",
            "Where is IOrderRepository registered, and what's it wired to?",
            "Trace DI registrations scans the project for Add/TryAdd/AddKeyed calls referencing the type and returns a compact table of file:line, lifetime, and service → implementation — the wiring a constructor search can't surface.",
            50, 80),

        new("C# minify (Roslyn)",
            ".cs",
            "Read OrderService.cs and explain how status transitions work.",
            "Minify C# file uses Roslyn to strip comments and XML docs, collapses whitespace — every line of logic preserved. Right when the question spans the whole file rather than one method.",
            20, 50),

        new("C# minify (universal)",
            ".csproj .props .config .xml",
            "Read App.csproj — why is this package reference here?",
            "Minify file auto-dispatches by extension. For non-C# types it uses a lexical stripper — same concept, no Roslyn dependency.",
            20, 40),

        new("Razor",
            ".razor",
            "Translate this Blazor page to React.",
            "Returns both the minified markup and the @code C# in two labeled sections.",
            25, 50),

        new("XML / .NET projects",
            ".csproj .props .config .xml",
            "Look at App.csproj — why is this NuGet reference here?",
            "Strips <!-- --> comments and collapses blank-line runs.",
            20, 40),

        // ----- Additional: basic minification, not actively tested -----
        new("JavaScript / TypeScript",
            ".js .ts .jsx .tsx",
            "Read this React component and add a loading state.",
            "Lexical strip of comments and whitespace, strings and template literals preserved.",
            30, 50, Primary: false),

        new("Python",
            ".py",
            "Explain what this Python script does and add type hints.",
            "Strips # comments, keeps docstrings and indentation intact.",
            25, 45, Primary: false),

        new("HTML",
            ".html .htm",
            "Look at index.html and tell me where to add the analytics script.",
            "Strips HTML comments, collapses attribute spacing.",
            20, 40, Primary: false),

        new("CSS / SCSS / LESS",
            ".css .scss .less",
            "Why is this stylesheet so big? Audit it.",
            "Strips /* */ comments and whitespace. Bigger savings on heavily-commented design systems.",
            10, 40, Primary: false),

        new("JSON / JSONC",
            ".json .jsonc",
            "What does this tsconfig.json do?",
            "Collapses pretty-printed JSON and strips // and /* */ comments (JSONC).",
            30, 50, Primary: false),

        new("YAML",
            ".yaml .yml",
            "Read this docker-compose.yml and explain the service graph.",
            "Strips # comments, preserves indentation (YAML is indent-sensitive).",
            20, 40, Primary: false),
    };

    private static string SavingsTier(int high) =>
        high >= 70 ? "tier-high"
      : high >= 45 ? "tier-mid"
      : "tier-low";
}
